hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us. H Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Abu Usama told us. H Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us, all of them, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, my father told me, on the authority of Humran Ibn Aban, that he informed, he said: I saw Othman Ibn Affan called for ablution, so he performed ablution on the court, and he said: I will narrate to you a hadith that I heard from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well and prays, will be forgiven.” He has what comes between it and the other prayer.” This is the wording of the hadith of Yahya bin Saeed"
